  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the female police officer as the agent of retaliation",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the female police officer (visual material) as the embodiment of the violent response being called for. The text 'well ladies, it's time to lock and load' directly addresses 'ladies' (women), suggesting the user (or the audience) is being invited to identify with or act through the female officer as a figure of authority and retaliation. The officer is the focal point and the visual representation of the 'lock and load' command, making her the projected entity onto which the user's identity or action is mapped.",
